racy\">The Temple of Silence</a>- a tradition coming from the first and only rebellion of Irem who worship a Named Goddess who was punished for her part in the rebellion and seeks to give the Nameless Empire its proper burial<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/600502-maw-of-the-river-mummy-hunters\">Maw of the River</a>- assassins who devour the relics of the past in order to return them to the River of Time and seeks to destroy all which was left of Irem's legacy while chasing down the Devourer and her spawn.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/584777-maagal-habaal-vehaashera-dark-eras-book-of-judges\">Maagal HaBaal VeHaAshera</a>- biblical idol makers turned into modern artists who shape Sekhem in order to give life to their gods while fighting against the attempts of the Deathless at destroying their creations and stealing their secrets.<br /> <br /> more groups, which are more loosely connected to those enemies, could be found in my sig.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMPRESSIVE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T05:01:57-08:00","id":784064,"title":"","content":"Mummies also have Last Dynasty, who are set up sympathetically enough to be playable but, I don't think, have any mechanical difference from normal humans, although you could probably whip something up involving their Sekhem-harvesting and Amkhata-making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T06:11:05-08:00","id":784108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/782806-mummies-and-prometheans-and-geists-oh-my?p=784064#post784064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies also have Last Dynasty, who are set up sympathetically enough to be playable but, I don't think, have any mechanical difference from normal humans, although you could probably whip something up involving their Sekhem-harvesting and Amkhata-making.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, I've also made an Endowment for them (which is based more around Srkhem Harvesting than Amkhata creation) in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2?p=633773#post633773\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:28:11-08:00","id":787069,"title":"","content":"I was bouncing around the idea of an Orthodox Jewish compact that deals primarily with prometheans (golems) and ghosts/spirits. It would be largely disorganized and carried through word of mouth through insular communities, but I'm also picturing a small network of &quot;fixers&quot; who are contracted out for situations that get out of control. I'm just not sure I have the credibility to do the idea justice. I'm figuring a group that, for a long time was essentially a loose information trade among spiritual leaders in Hasidic communities but has since been overtaken more by seedier elements (influenced by the real life story of Rabbi Mendel Epstein's black hat goon squad and the orthodox mafia elements in The Yiddish Policemen's Union), a small group of rough men who deal with problems of supernatural threat in communities that are reticent to go to secular authorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 12-15-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}